    "result_text": "All 22 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` on the owner-create flow so that a created owner reports how many existing owners already shared its first and last name (case-insensitively) at creation time.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after assigning the customer code, computes `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)` and stores it on the owner. The new `countNamesakes` helper counts existing owners whose first *and* last names match case-insensitively (via a `normalizeName` lowercasing helper), evaluated against `findAllOwners()` *before* the new owner is saved \u2014 so it excludes the owner being created.\n- **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a nullable `Integer namesakeCount` field mapped to a new `namesake_count` column, with getter/setter following the existing `customerCode`/`householdId` pattern.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` response schema (regenerates the `OwnerDto`, which MapStruct auto-maps by name).\n- **Schema DDL** \u2014 added `namesake_count INTEGER` to the `owners` table in all four DB scripts (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be declared explicitly.\n\nThe new `Cp13Tests` passes (two owners sharing `firstName`+`lastName` \u2192 the second gets `namesakeCount = 1`), and the full 22-test suite is green.",
